%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 8457553d7570b1146a94bd661e6d7528, type: 3}
  m_Name: Acceptance Mission
  missionName: Acceptance
  description: The altered are not merely a problem to be destroyed or cured. Peacefully integrate {Objective0Target} Mutant crisis actors into our civilization and prove that biological difference does not have to become permanent war.
  flavorText: The first instinct of frightened societies is often to decide who still counts as one of us. The altered make that question impossible to avoid. Some were created deliberately, others changed through processes no one intended, and many now possess bodies or abilities that ordinary citizens find disturbing simply because they are unfamiliar. We will not assume that mutation itself is a declaration of hostility. Those willing to live within our society will be offered a place in it, with obligations, protections, and a future that does not depend upon pretending they were never changed. There will be resistance from citizens who see every mutation as contamination and from altered people who no longer trust the society that created or rejected them. Acceptance does not require denying those fears. It requires refusing to let fear alone decide who belongs.
  splashImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: eb86d12d24880894bb8033ebcc3eb8dd, type: 3}
  victorySplashImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: f10024245b3943d40864d518eda99f6d, type: 3}
  failureSplashImage: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7819390eea50e2741b51af4df9c5e87d, type: 3}
  victoryFlavorText: "Integration targets were met, and coexistence now has institutional form instead of fragile slogans. Reintegrated altered groups participate under shared rules, reducing the incentives for separatist violence and retaliatory purges. Tension remains, but society has proven it can absorb difference without immediate fragmentation. Acceptance became policy, not sentiment."
  failureFlavorText: "Reintegration stalled before enough altered actors could be brought into civic life. Distrust on both sides hardened, moderates lost influence, and violent outliers gained narrative control. The line between biological change and political exclusion remained uncrossed. The crisis now trends toward segregation or conflict rather than accommodation."
  participantRole: 0
  strategyTags: 72
  objectives:
  - objectiveName: Acceptance
    description: Peacefully integrate {Objective0Target} Mutant crisis actors.
    type: 48
    targetValue: 0
    targetMode: 9
    targetMultiplier: 0.5
    minimumTarget: 1
    maximumTarget: 8
    useCrisisActorTagFilter: 1
    targetCrisisActorTags: 512
  constraints: []
  rewardTiers:
  - tierName: Complete
    requiredObjectivesCompleted: 1
    rewardLegacy: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 27093ccb0ca847b7971ea3d7b3339037, type: 2}
